{"ts": 0.074312, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mWhere you are\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA folder can hold files and other folders. You are always standing\r\nin one folder; the shell calls it the \u001b[1mcurrent directory\u001b[0m.\r\nYour practice folder looks like this:\r\n\r\n  /var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-vsjmn_82\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m◀ you are here\u001b[0m\r\n  ├── poem.txt\r\n  ├── numbers.txt\r\n", "len": 362}
{"ts": 0.074383, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  ├── stage1/\r\n  └── stage2/\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mpwd\u001b[0m prints the name of the current directory.\r\nPredict what it will print, then run it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[93m, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 205}
{"ts": 0.077879, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 71}
