{"ts": 0.166557, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mNames for places\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short names point at places in the tree you have seen:\r\n  \u001b[1m.\u001b[0m    here, the current directory\r\n  \u001b[1m..\u001b[0m   one level up, the parent\r\n  \u001b[1m~\u001b[0m    your home folder\r\n\r\nA \u001b[1mpath\u001b[0m names a place. \u001b[1mRelative\u001b[0m paths start where you are:\r\n", "len": 288}
{"ts": 0.166603, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[90mpractice/notes.txt\u001b[0m   a file inside a subfolder\r\n  \u001b[90m../notes.txt\u001b[0m         a file in the parent folder\r\n\u001b[1mAbsolute\u001b[0m paths start from the root, \u001b[1m/\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[90m/etc/hosts\u001b[0m   \u001b[90m/usr/bin/vim\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[91mPredict before you act.\u001b[0m  In \u001b[90m~/projects\u001b[0m, the bare name \u001b[90mnotes\u001b[0m means \u001b[90m~/projects/notes\u001b[0m.\r\n  \u001b[92mmkdir name\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m# make a folder called name, right here\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try \u001b[92mmkdir demo\u001b[93m, \u001b[92mls -p\u001b[93m, then \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 501}
